From f82349167052b0db60bc461b7418a0401a643861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Arango <95070226+ja-818@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Admit the J716s (apple,j716s) in developer builds:
 experimental, one machine

The 16-inch MacBook Pro with M5 Pro (Mac17,8, J716s, board 0x0c, T6050)
as a developer-only board, for one owner's test (ja-818). Not booted yet.

Apple's 27.2 restore image (26B123) already carries the J716s: its
j716sap identities (ApBoardID 0x0C, ApChipID 0x6050, iBoot.j716s
mBoot-20457.41.3) name the same DCP (t605xdcp), GPU (armfw_g17x), ANE,
AVE and AOP firmware, by digest, as the j714sap ones, and the same N1
FTAB (t2026macG1, Wireless1 chip 0x2026, board 2113). The release 9
kernel package already ships t6050-j716s.dtb (aurora-silicon/linux
677be395, #1167).

- Engine: j716sap device (27.2, expert off), j716sap on the 26B123 row
  beside j714sap, and the board 0x0c gate. BOARD_MACHO j716sap takes the
  J714s image's own Stage 1 members (stage1-j714s.{bin,macho}): Stage 1 is
  chip-level and only chainloads the ESP Stage 2, whose device trees
  include t6050-j716s.dtb. The image is bound to the board by its
  installer_data (allowed_device_classes [j716sap]), so a J714s image is
  still refused on a J716s and back.
- Centauri: the N1 FTAB is ticketed for j716sap/0x0c as for j714sap/0x08
  (apple/centauri/j716s-ftab.bin, the name the J716s device tree asks for).
- supported-models.json: apple,j716s as a developer board; MacModelNames:
  J716s; test_make_unsigned_catalog: the developer board set.
- Tests: the J716s board row, its Mach-O Stage 1 install, the refusals
  (J714s image on a J716s and back, wrong firmware, mixed metadata,
  missing members), the 26B123 row for j716sap, the Centauri ticket for
  j716sap and its board refusals.
- Engine v0.9.2-omarchy.20261121.7aeda1cfee47 (engine_pin.py name),
  rebuilt with rebuild-python-overlay.py from the authenticated engine.28
  base: 17915198 bytes, sha256
  4316cc91f79b6aa24a5056147710f2127736d50d114e2dec3fbb78ad0dee7480, two
  identical rebuilds, prepare-engine.py reproduces it.

Checked: engine overlay tests (448, 27 skips), scripts tests
test_make_unsigned_catalog (40), ./test/all (portable checks passed),
engine_pin.py check, prepare-engine.py. Not run: nothing here has been
booted on a J716s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
